Z||000008||V6pack||03-14-2000||11:04 PM||||Whoa...Heard enough...I'm with you Motorhead!  William T.T. III...I usually keep my mouth shut, fight my own battles, and take my lumps. <P>But....as long as you have your checkbook out you can send me the $100 refund (or the product I waited for) for....let's see now, I guess this is the 55th day.  <P>I have received the first $100. in check form(not the promised MO)for half of the promised $200. refund,but it has yet to clear.  So maybe you could guarantee that one too.... in case it doesn't clear... especially now.  <P>If a vendor actively solicits orders here and then promises refunds on those same unfilled orders....the customer has a right to expect the refund to arrive soon after it is promised.<P>There are more than just two of us in need....but we all looked at that heartwarming "farewell"... apparently "semi retirement" thread and decided not to say anything for fear of being stiffed for speaking our minds.  But, since this person told my lady he "would just sit back and laugh" if we went to the list for leverage I have decided to air it here tonight. <P>Nearing two months now and I have lost all patience and I am willing to take the risk that half or all of my $200. is lost.  The next to last straw came when the vendor wrote here about picking up sub parts and other goodies. I can't speak for Motorhead, but I wondered how he could continue to buy and sell when he could not/would not send refunds out.<P>I have a feeling you may want to beef up your checking account W.T.T.III.  I'd love to send you ALL the e-mail I have saved regarding my experience with this vendor!!!   Write me and I will send all of the supporting documentation. <P>There have been various threads on all the lists warning about "iffy" vendors.  This is the forum of first and last resort.  I found this vendor here, and this is where I will leave him... so it is entirely appropriate to air these problems here.<P>Motorhead may have exausted his patience, and I agree with him that if we can't get our $ back, then we are compelled to inform the list.  We owe listers the opportunity to avoid the same run-around we have both received.  You can also assume that I have begged, pleaded, and threatened to the point that I finally gave it to the little lady to handle. The lousy response she got from this vendor pissed me off....so here I am!  <P>If it were me I would borrow the money and "overnight" it with profuse apologies. I would even include a peace offering to save the custom and good word of mouth.<P>Oh, by the way...both of my parents are very ill and I am recently disabled ...with two kids and NO job.  <P>Before the flames, please imagine it was your $ and too many days of "reasonable" effort had been made.  Then, ask yourself ... what you would do?  <P>I apologize for the long post and know that I will offend some of you.  I don't say much on the forum...just listen, learn, and buy.  I am just sharing what I have learned about this particular Fiero related experience....and offer it as money saving tip meant to inform other unsuspecting, trusting, Fiero enthusiest.<BR>v6pack<P><BR>||||reg||9
Z||000009||TOM||03-14-2000||11:57 PM||||MOTORHEAD. I havent sent a refund because I was trying to get you the part. I didnt know you found one. Maybe you should have let me know.<P>V6 Why have you not cashed it yet. And thanks for letting me know you had even received it. <BR>It people like you guys that make me not want to do fiero parts anymore. I hope neither of you ever have a loss like I have recently experienced. No wait I take that back. I hope you do, and very soon.||||reg||1
