Z||000014||william_thorniii||03-15-2000||04:49 PM||||Gentlemen,<P>Please lets at least try to keep this civil.  <P>V6Pack & Moterhead,<P>Your explanations were very well thought out and did shed some light on your experience.  I am truly sorry that I ever got in this thread.  That does not mean that I agree with you, but can understand some of your frustration.  <P>I would tentatively suggest a deviation from this plan of action in the future.  When faced with a dilema that appears insurmountable on ones own, I do not see a problem with starting a thread on the Forum.  If handled properly, all could go away from such a situation happier.  I cannot imagine this mix up to be more than just that a mix up.  Effective communication is the key to a good community.  <P>I don't think that anyone really wants you two to leave, but one thing is certain... many folks definitely don't want to see Tom and his wonderful service (to the rest of us) go.  Tom has helped many people in many ways, often at little or no profit to himself.  It will truly be a sad day if he were in fact to leave the Forum.  <P>I am only trying to help... but confess that I don't really know how.  Any suggestions?<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
